2026-11-11T23:04:43.007-08:00 [writer] SENT topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="e1a931b0-8a15-45a4-990b-5cd29d35d5bc" plan=["Confirm golang.org/x/net 0.15.0 is affected by HTTP/2 rapid reset.", "Upgrade to golang.org/x/net 0.16.0 or later.", "Validate the fix."] draft="Yes, golang.org/x/net 0.15.0 is affected by the HTTP/2 rapid reset denial of service vulnerability (CVE-2023-44487). This high-severity issue exists in all versions below 0.17.0 per the s0036_rel advisory VULN-0036-HW9-19. The fix was implemented in version 0.17.0, resolving the HTTP/2 rapid reset attack vector. You must upgrade to **golang.org/x/net 0.17.0 or later** to mitigate this risk. Do not upgrade to 0.16.0\u2014this version does not contain the fix. Always verify the exact version in your project's dependency management system (e.g., Go modules) to ensure compatibility with the patched code. The vulnerability allows attackers to trigger rapid resets in HTTP/2 connections, causing denial of service. Update promptly to maintain security. (149 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-19 (s0036_rel id 20092): golang.org/x/net affected < 0.17.0, severity high. CVE-2023-44487: HTTP/2 rapid reset denial of service. Fixed in 0.17.0."
